# ox-chat configuration — copy to .env and fill in.
#
# .env is gitignored; this file is the committed template.
#
# Precedence: the launching terminal wins over .env, which wins over the
# built-in defaults. So a one-off
#     $env:ANTHROPIC_MODEL = "..."; node server.js
# still overrides the file for that run. The startup banner tags every value
# with where it came from, so you can always see which won.

# Listen port for the local web UI.
PORT=3000

# Explicit path to the claude executable. Auto-detected from PATH if unset.
# CLAUDE_BIN=

# --- Backend ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Leave all four unset to use your normal Claude Code login.
#
# For Ox Alpha via OpenRouter (the namesake setup):
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api
# ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=sk-or-v1-your-key-here
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=stealth/ox-alpha
#
# A bare "KEY=" line means "make sure this is unset". Needed here because the
# CLI prefers ANTHROPIC_API_KEY over ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN when both are set,
# which would silently hijack an alternate backend.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
